/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Write the input as a phasor Vin and the output as Vout.
   - For the RC low-pass, take the output across C.
   - H(jω) = 1 / (1 + jωRC), |H| = 1 / √(1 + (ωRC)²), φ = −arctan(ωRC)
   - Here ω is angular frequency in rad/s; R is resistance in Ω; C is capacitance in F; |H| is gain; φ is output phase minus input phase in degrees.
   - The cutoff is where ωRC = 1.
   - The first-order RL low-pass has the same shape with time constant L/R.
   - Take the output across R.
   - H(jω) = jωRC / (1 + jωRC), |H| = ωRC / √(1 + (ωRC)²), φ = 90° − arctan(ωRC)
   - Here ωc = 1/(RC) is the cutoff; at ω = ωc the gain is 0.707 and the phase is +45°.
   - A high-pass RC removes DC and low-frequency hum.
*/
