/* book exam traps: The impedance locus with R varied is a straight line, but the current locus is a circle. Do not draw the current as a line. | Diameter slip: with R varied the diameter is V/X; with X varied it is V/R. The diameter is always V over the element that stays fixed. | Half-plane: an RL current lags and is drawn below V; an RC current leads and is drawn above V. A locus on the wrong side earns no marks. | Two resonant values of XL exist only when XC > 2R. Check the discriminant before quoting two answers. | Maximum power with R varied comes at R = |X| (the 45° point), and Pmax = V²/(2|X|); it is not at R = 0, where the current is largest. */
